# static/tailwind.css was ignored here until 2026-08-30. It is COMMITTED now, on
# purpose: base.html has linked it since the design-system port, nothing ever built
# it, and `make css` assumed a global `tailwindcss` binary that no instruction
# installs -- so every clone rendered the management pages unstyled. Shipping the
# built file is what makes `git clone && uv sync && ./run-sidecar.sh` produce a
# working app with no Node toolchain, and it matches the vendored htmx.min.js next
# to it. Rebuild with `make css` after changing input.css.


# Extraction ground-truth corpus: raw article HTML is real feed content and must
# never be committed to this public repo. The manifest + fetch_fixtures.py (both
# committed) repopulate this on demand; the corpus tests skip when it's absent.
tests/fixtures/extraction/_raw/
